1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:06,000
Healthy routines break when the week changes.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:11,800
Generic reminders neither know you nor explain why.

3
00:00:11,900 --> 00:00:17,600
One sentence in, a reviewed record out.

4
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:23,400
Check in, review, passport, Inclinations, next step. Pain or crisis goes to a person.

5
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:27,800
A synthetic check-in starts as one plain sentence.

6
00:00:27,800 --> 00:00:32,800
It proposes 3 values, each with the words it came from. Mood gave none.

7
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:36,800
Sleep is corrected to 6.5 hours; the other two are confirmed.

8
00:00:36,800 --> 00:00:39,600
Nothing is saved until the review is submitted.

9
00:00:39,680 --> 00:00:44,380
Saved values update the Health Clone Passport.

10
00:00:44,380 --> 00:00:49,380
The evidence thread traces one value from the check-in to the card.

11
00:00:49,380 --> 00:00:53,580
A card with no value in 14 days is withheld, not guessed.

12
00:00:53,750 --> 00:00:59,450
Inclinations: what weighs most for this member, from 7 short questions (simulated answers).

13
00:00:59,450 --> 00:01:05,850
Each next step is linked to one of them, with its reason. A prompt for the care team, not a care plan.

14
00:01:05,990 --> 00:01:09,690
After a pain report, the next step routes to a person.

15
00:01:09,690 --> 00:01:13,090
The person can choose, defer or ask a professional.

16
00:01:13,200 --> 00:01:17,400
Crisis language is not processed.

17
00:01:17,400 --> 00:01:21,700
A fixed hand-off points to a person. Nothing is saved.

18
00:01:21,880 --> 00:01:27,680
The timeline shows what each saved check-in changed.

19
00:01:27,760 --> 00:01:32,960
The research console leads with its results, in plain language.

20
00:01:32,960 --> 00:01:37,860
Training runs offline. No AI model is used in the check-in loop.

21
00:01:37,990 --> 00:01:43,190
Each training step was tested on the same 141 held-out practice prompts.

22
00:01:43,190 --> 00:01:49,430
With simulated members, the learned approach logged 84.0% of days, against 83.3% for the best fixed one.

23
00:01:49,330 --> 00:01:55,530
Rules run live, with no model call in the check-in loop.

24
00:01:55,530 --> 00:02:01,830
Training and evaluation run offline and publish versioned results.

25
00:02:01,930 --> 00:02:08,630
Memory keeps only what the person confirmed.

26
00:02:08,630 --> 00:02:15,430
The boundary rules caught 74 of 74 labelled violations, with 0 false alarms on 128 rows.

27
00:02:15,530 --> 00:02:21,230
7 answers recover each hidden trait 76–91% of the time.

28
00:02:21,230 --> 00:02:26,730
The reward model reads term by term; its top message type matches for 83%.

29
00:02:26,730 --> 00:02:32,030
GRPO learns which message type to send.

30
00:02:32,130 --> 00:02:37,830
On 141 held-out prompts, the base model passed 45.

31
00:02:37,830 --> 00:02:42,830
Both trained stages passed all 141.

32
00:02:42,830 --> 00:02:47,630
The learned policy reached 0.840 mean simulated adherence, against 0.833 for the best script.

33
00:02:47,730 --> 00:02:53,930
Next: a clinical reviewer, a consented pilot, a measured result.

34
00:02:53,930 --> 00:03:00,030
The prototype and this deck are live at the demo link.
